1
00:00:42,647 --> 00:00:46,067
SOLD OUT ON YOU

2
00:01:05,253 --> 00:01:07,797
Ms. Dam, what are you doing?
Didn't you hear the car?

3
00:01:21,978 --> 00:01:22,812
Are you okay?

4
00:01:24,606 --> 00:01:27,942
Ms. Dam, are you drunk?

5
00:01:38,745 --> 00:01:40,079
Ms. Dam.

6
00:02:08,816 --> 00:02:10,193
Stay here for a moment.

7
00:02:21,246 --> 00:02:22,247
Thank you.

8
00:05:21,717 --> 00:05:22,718
Ms. Dam…

9
00:05:40,987 --> 00:05:41,821
Mr. Mechoori?

10
00:05:48,953 --> 00:05:49,871
What are you…

11
00:06:09,682 --> 00:06:10,641
I like it.

12
00:06:17,190 --> 00:06:19,442
What cologne do you use?

13
00:06:19,942 --> 00:06:22,278
What do you think you're doing?

14
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:30,161
That subtle yet nonchalant scent
of woody musk…

15
00:06:31,954 --> 00:06:35,416
I think our customers
would really love this.

16
00:06:37,126 --> 00:06:38,294
I'm not using any cologne.

17
00:06:45,009 --> 00:06:46,594
You want it just for yourself?

18
00:06:51,599 --> 00:06:52,683
You're such a jerk.

19
00:06:56,354 --> 00:06:57,688
You little…

20
00:06:57,772 --> 00:06:58,773
Ms. Dam…

21
00:09:06,609 --> 00:09:08,361
I'm all out.

22
00:09:17,953 --> 00:09:19,163
When did I scratch my foot?

23
00:09:21,123 --> 00:09:22,249
That hurts.

24
00:10:19,807 --> 00:10:21,016
Mom.

25
00:10:22,601 --> 00:10:24,311
Pick up.

26
00:10:25,479 --> 00:10:26,981
Please pick up.

27
00:11:19,033 --> 00:11:19,867
Hey, Mechoori!

28
00:11:22,620 --> 00:11:23,871
Hey, Som-yi.

29
00:11:23,954 --> 00:11:26,707
Shouldn't you be going to school now?
Is something wrong?

30
00:11:26,790 --> 00:11:28,334
Well,

31
00:11:28,417 --> 00:11:30,169
it's not that…

32
00:11:31,921 --> 00:11:32,922
Do you have any money?

33
00:11:34,507 --> 00:11:35,382
How much do you need?

34
00:11:35,466 --> 00:11:39,428
Jin-yi said she'd give me 50,000 won
if I help clean the shop next week.

35
00:11:40,596 --> 00:11:41,931
You want me to lend you 50,000?

36
00:11:42,014 --> 00:11:44,141
What are you going to use it for?

37
00:11:44,225 --> 00:11:45,059
"Poca"!

38
00:11:47,937 --> 00:11:48,854
What did you just say?

39
00:11:51,732 --> 00:11:53,442
Poker? You…

40
00:11:55,069 --> 00:11:56,278
I can't let you do that.

41
00:11:56,362 --> 00:11:57,821
Why not? That's my joy in life.

42
00:11:57,905 --> 00:11:59,031
Som-yi!

43
00:11:59,782 --> 00:12:02,535
Look, there are a lot
of good and fun hobbies to do.

44
00:12:02,618 --> 00:12:04,662
If you get addicted,
it'll be hard to quit.

45
00:12:05,246 --> 00:12:06,872
In any case, I can't let you gamble.

46
00:12:08,165 --> 00:12:09,083
What are you on about?

47
00:12:12,169 --> 00:12:13,462
I meant photo cards.

48
00:12:13,546 --> 00:12:15,339
I'm going to buy photo cards.

49
00:12:15,422 --> 00:12:16,715
Photo cards?

50
00:12:20,636 --> 00:12:21,470
Photo cards?

51
00:12:23,138 --> 00:12:24,139
You want 50,000 won?

52
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:27,434
Mechoori.

53
00:12:27,518 --> 00:12:29,186
Instead of working today,

54
00:12:29,270 --> 00:12:31,564
why don't you go online
and study the outside world?

55
00:12:32,481 --> 00:12:33,649
DAM YE-JIN

56
00:12:37,444 --> 00:12:39,530
Mechoori, are you "stanning" her?

57
00:12:39,613 --> 00:12:40,573
No.

58
00:12:41,448 --> 00:12:42,658
What's "stanning"?

59
00:12:42,741 --> 00:12:43,742
Do you like her?

60
00:12:43,826 --> 00:12:45,202
No!

61
00:12:46,412 --> 00:12:49,290
I mean, something about her
was just bothering me a bit.

62
00:12:50,374 --> 00:12:52,459
That's how stanning starts.

63
00:12:53,919 --> 00:12:55,629
You want something to eat, Som-yi?

64
00:13:07,641 --> 00:13:08,475
Damn it.

65
00:13:08,559 --> 00:13:11,145
-This is bad news for Jin-yi.
-What?

66
00:13:12,730 --> 00:13:13,856
It's nothing.

67
00:13:14,773 --> 00:13:16,191
She seems fine this morning though.

68
00:13:17,860 --> 00:13:18,944
How would you know?

69
00:13:19,028 --> 00:13:20,154
She's doing a live now.

70
00:13:20,237 --> 00:13:21,196
A "live"?

71
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:22,698
A live broadcast!

72
00:13:22,781 --> 00:13:25,242
<i>Hello. Good morning.</i>

73
00:13:25,826 --> 00:13:26,660
<i>Everyone.</i>

74
00:13:27,745 --> 00:13:29,997
<i>Look at the sky. Isn't it beautiful?</i>

75
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:33,626
This is my favorite spot
by the Hangang River.

76
00:13:33,709 --> 00:13:36,003
I feel so refreshed when I come here.

77
00:13:36,503 --> 00:13:38,881
I started a live
so you all could see this too.

78
00:13:38,964 --> 00:13:42,760
<i>But it doesn't even look</i>
<i>half as good on camera.</i>

79
00:13:43,510 --> 00:13:45,929
<i>The weather? It's already hot.</i>

80
00:13:46,013 --> 00:13:49,808
Are you curious whether she slept well

81
00:13:50,559 --> 00:13:52,102
or if she made sure to eat her meals?

82
00:13:52,645 --> 00:13:54,271
I told you it's not like that.

83
00:13:54,772 --> 00:13:56,607
Come on, Uncle Mechoori.

84
00:14:01,779 --> 00:14:05,949
Was there a mistake with the last fitting?
It's so tight around the waist.

85
00:14:06,450 --> 00:14:08,285
We didn't change anything.

86
00:14:10,454 --> 00:14:12,039
Have you gained weight?

87
00:14:12,122 --> 00:14:13,374
Come on.

88
00:14:13,916 --> 00:14:16,669
You know I stay on a strict diet
before my shows.

89
00:14:17,836 --> 00:14:19,046
Why is this so tight?

90
00:14:22,883 --> 00:14:24,343
It's not much, but eat up.

91
00:14:26,512 --> 00:14:28,764
Here are the potatoes you like.
I grew these myself.

92
00:14:28,847 --> 00:14:31,433
Have some <i>sikhye</i> to help it go down nice.

93
00:14:37,022 --> 00:14:38,649
But I only had a bite of each dish…

94
00:14:38,732 --> 00:14:39,692
It's only on Saturdays.

95
00:14:39,775 --> 00:14:40,901
-Seriously.
-No way.

96
00:14:40,985 --> 00:14:43,195
-I mean it!
-You're starting to get on my nerves!

97
00:14:43,278 --> 00:14:44,738
Nice outfit today.

98
00:14:46,824 --> 00:14:48,450
Is it a bit small?

99
00:14:50,369 --> 00:14:51,286
No, it isn't.

100
00:14:52,413 --> 00:14:55,249
I'd like to change to heels
that cover my feet.

101
00:14:56,333 --> 00:14:57,960
-Let's see…
-What happened to your feet?

102
00:14:58,043 --> 00:14:59,044
Did you hurt yourself?

103
00:15:00,004 --> 00:15:02,923
I don't know. I woke up like this.
I guess I scratched them somewhere.

104
00:15:03,007 --> 00:15:05,467
How would that happen in your sleep?
You sure you're okay?

105
00:15:05,551 --> 00:15:08,470
I'm actually doing very well these days,
so don't worry.

106
00:15:09,221 --> 00:15:11,765
But what were you chatting about?
You sounded so excited.

107
00:15:11,849 --> 00:15:12,725
Well…

108
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:14,727
Ms. Dam!

109
00:15:14,810 --> 00:15:16,103
Geez.

110
00:15:16,186 --> 00:15:17,229
What? What is it?

111
00:15:17,312 --> 00:15:19,231
We have news, and it's big news.

112
00:15:19,314 --> 00:15:23,402
We asked for as much storage as possible
for L'Étoile's essence,

113
00:15:23,485 --> 00:15:26,405
and they actually emptied out
an entire warehouse for us!

114
00:15:26,488 --> 00:15:28,449
An entire warehouse?

115
00:15:28,532 --> 00:15:30,743
Just thinking of filling
that warehouse with essence

116
00:15:30,826 --> 00:15:32,453
is giving me a dopamine rush!

117
00:15:32,536 --> 00:15:33,579
A huge rush!

118
00:15:33,662 --> 00:15:35,956
You might just set a new record

119
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:37,916
for the highest sales
in the shortest time!

120
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,376
A new record!

121
00:15:40,044 --> 00:15:42,463
Are talks going smoothly
with Gojeuneok Bio?

122
00:15:42,546 --> 00:15:44,048
Why would you even ask that?

123
00:15:44,131 --> 00:15:45,257
Don't you know Ye-jin?

124
00:15:45,340 --> 00:15:47,843
Tell Mr. Seo to gather
all the essence they can provide.

125
00:15:47,926 --> 00:15:49,178
And you'll sell all of them.

126
00:15:49,261 --> 00:15:50,387
Yes, everything.

127
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:08,113
AN ENTIRE WAREHOUSE EMPTIED OUT

128
00:16:13,160 --> 00:16:14,453
Mr. Mechoori!

129
00:16:14,536 --> 00:16:16,371
No. I mean, Mr. Matthew Lee!

130
00:16:16,455 --> 00:16:18,624
I'm in huge trouble. Please help me out.

131
00:16:19,416 --> 00:16:22,419
Mr. Lee! Please help me!

132
00:16:22,503 --> 00:16:24,963
I swear I won't ask for a favor
like this again! Please!

133
00:16:25,047 --> 00:16:27,091
If you help me out just this once…

134
00:16:32,387 --> 00:16:33,972
GO BACK. THERE ARE NO MUSHROOMS

135
00:16:35,557 --> 00:16:37,142
Mechoori… I mean, Mr. Matthew Lee.

136
00:16:37,226 --> 00:16:39,853
Sir, please help me out just this once!

137
00:16:39,937 --> 00:16:41,438
NO. LEAVE

138
00:16:41,522 --> 00:16:43,232
GO AWAY

139
00:16:43,315 --> 00:16:45,150
YOU WEREN'T CONSIDERATE OF ME

140
00:16:46,401 --> 00:16:48,445
THESE ARE THE CONSEQUENCES

141
00:16:48,529 --> 00:16:49,530
Those wings are gross!

142
00:16:49,613 --> 00:16:51,406
No, I didn't mean that. I'm sorry.

143
00:16:51,490 --> 00:16:53,659
I'm sorry. I take that back.
Please forgive me!

144
00:16:55,577 --> 00:16:57,204
DARN IT

145
00:16:58,956 --> 00:17:00,290
YOU WON'T EVEN SEE THE MUSHROOMS

146
00:17:00,374 --> 00:17:02,292
LET ME BE CLEAR

147
00:17:02,376 --> 00:17:06,130
YOU'LL NEVER BE ABLE TO SEE
MY MUSHROOMS AGAIN

148
00:17:06,213 --> 00:17:08,423
GOODBYE!

149
00:17:08,507 --> 00:17:11,051
Mr. Lee, please come back! Don't leave!

150
00:17:11,927 --> 00:17:13,512
Right! I'm Dam Ye-jin.

151
00:17:13,595 --> 00:17:16,807
Of course! Don't worry,
and secure as much stock as you can!

152
00:17:16,890 --> 00:17:19,726
Get as much as you want!
We'll support you all the way. Got that?

153
00:17:22,020 --> 00:17:24,690
You two are so reliable.

154
00:17:27,151 --> 00:17:28,443
I have an urgent meeting.

155
00:17:36,410 --> 00:17:40,122
Granny, what do we do about Jin-yi now?

156
00:17:40,747 --> 00:17:42,583
She's going to lose Mechoori
to someone else.

157
00:17:43,333 --> 00:17:45,335
Why? What's wrong with Jin-yi?

158
00:17:45,419 --> 00:17:48,547
My sister has no chance against her.

159
00:17:48,630 --> 00:17:50,716
What's on the inside matters more.

160
00:17:51,383 --> 00:17:55,262
Then, who do you think is prettier?
Jin-yi or Dam Ye-jin?

161
00:17:56,471 --> 00:17:57,764
-Jin.
-What?

162
00:17:58,515 --> 00:18:00,184
Dam Ye-jin.

163
00:18:00,267 --> 00:18:02,769
She does have a bright and lovely smile.

164
00:18:02,853 --> 00:18:03,937
Granny!

165
00:18:09,693 --> 00:18:11,069
Hey, sweetie.

166
00:18:11,820 --> 00:18:13,113
-Mechoori?
-Mechoori?

167
00:18:14,364 --> 00:18:16,825
Why are you asking about Mechoori?
Who are you?

168
00:18:16,909 --> 00:18:18,327
Me? I'm Dam Ye-jin.

169
00:18:18,410 --> 00:18:19,494
<i>Who are you?</i>

170
00:18:22,080 --> 00:18:23,582
None of your business.

171
00:18:23,665 --> 00:18:26,960
Hey. Are you close with our Mechoori?

172
00:18:27,044 --> 00:18:29,504
"Our Mechoori"? Are you two close?

173
00:18:29,588 --> 00:18:31,423
Yes, we're very close!

174
00:18:32,716 --> 00:18:33,592
Really?

175
00:18:33,675 --> 00:18:36,011
Then, I guess you'll know
where he is right now.

176
00:18:36,637 --> 00:18:37,930
Why do you want to know?

177
00:18:38,013 --> 00:18:39,973
Because I'm on my way to see him.

178
00:18:40,057 --> 00:18:42,517
He's busy harvesting corn today.

179
00:18:42,601 --> 00:18:44,603
Corn? When? What time?

180
00:18:45,854 --> 00:18:48,690
Wait. You might not know that
even if you're close.

181
00:18:48,774 --> 00:18:49,691
Come on.

182
00:18:50,275 --> 00:18:53,320
I know Mechoori's entire schedule, okay?

183
00:18:53,904 --> 00:18:56,406
Is that so?
Then, let's discuss the details later.

184
00:18:59,326 --> 00:19:00,160
Why did she hang up?

185
00:19:02,162 --> 00:19:02,996
She hung up?

186
00:19:03,080 --> 00:19:04,289
She just hung up.

187
00:19:05,082 --> 00:19:05,916
Gosh…

188
00:19:13,924 --> 00:19:15,342
The home shopping host, Dam Ye-jin?

189
00:19:16,218 --> 00:19:17,844
So that was you. Hi.

190
00:19:19,596 --> 00:19:22,266
Where did you buy that mask though?

191
00:19:22,349 --> 00:19:24,476
It looks comfortable and nice.

192
00:19:24,559 --> 00:19:25,519
I didn't buy this.

193
00:19:25,602 --> 00:19:26,603
Really?

194
00:19:29,147 --> 00:19:31,149
But shouldn't you be in school
at this hour?

195
00:19:31,858 --> 00:19:34,569
I'm receiving life lessons from Granny.

196
00:19:34,653 --> 00:19:36,571
I'm earning experience from an elder.

197
00:19:37,906 --> 00:19:39,533
Then, how about this kind of experience?

198
00:19:41,201 --> 00:19:43,120
Let's begin our warmup. All right.

199
00:19:44,454 --> 00:19:47,457
<i>National exercise, start!</i>

200
00:19:47,541 --> 00:19:49,042
Okay, hurry on in here!

201
00:19:49,126 --> 00:19:50,794
<i>One, two, three,</i>

202
00:19:50,877 --> 00:19:54,089
<i>four, five, six, seven, eight…</i>

203
00:19:54,172 --> 00:19:55,674
Look at that!

204
00:19:55,757 --> 00:19:58,010
<i>Two, three, four, five, six.</i>

205
00:19:58,093 --> 00:20:00,595
You can look later. Come on and do this!

206
00:20:01,388 --> 00:20:02,889
Okay, the knees!

207
00:20:02,973 --> 00:20:06,852
<i>Three, four, five, six, seven, eight.</i>

208
00:20:06,935 --> 00:20:13,233
<i>Two, two, three, four, five,</i>
<i>six, seven, and arms!</i>

209
00:20:13,317 --> 00:20:17,029
<i>One, two, three, four, five, six…</i>

210
00:20:17,529 --> 00:20:18,947
Som-yi, what about school?

211
00:20:19,656 --> 00:20:20,490
What?

212
00:20:21,283 --> 00:20:22,117
What is this?

213
00:20:22,701 --> 00:20:23,535
Oh, right!

214
00:20:24,870 --> 00:20:28,248
It's been a long time, Mr. Lee.

215
00:20:28,332 --> 00:20:29,666
Goodness…

216
00:20:29,750 --> 00:20:30,959
Gracious.

217
00:20:33,128 --> 00:20:34,171
It's not what you think.

218
00:20:34,254 --> 00:20:36,715
I promise I'm not here
to pester you today.

219
00:20:38,342 --> 00:20:41,595
Ms. Yang said she's harvesting corn,
so I came to help out.

220
00:20:42,721 --> 00:20:43,972
Help harvest corn?

221
00:20:44,056 --> 00:20:46,016
Yes. I'm actually very good with my hands.

222
00:20:46,099 --> 00:20:48,185
It's fine. We have enough people.

223
00:20:48,268 --> 00:20:49,227
Come on.

224
00:20:49,728 --> 00:20:52,064
I bet you'll like it
when you see me working.

225
00:20:53,231 --> 00:20:56,068
<i>You'll like it.</i>

226
00:20:56,151 --> 00:20:57,569
I like it.

227
00:21:00,238 --> 00:21:01,740
Are you all right?

228
00:21:02,616 --> 00:21:05,952
Mr. Lee, you should take good care
of your health when you're busy.

229
00:21:06,536 --> 00:21:09,956
Don't worry about me.
You should be taking care of yourself.

230
00:21:10,707 --> 00:21:11,625
What?

231
00:21:11,708 --> 00:21:13,251
I mean…

232
00:21:13,335 --> 00:21:15,545
Mechoori! We're all waiting!

233
00:21:15,629 --> 00:21:16,463
Goodness.

234
00:21:17,297 --> 00:21:21,176
Okay, everyone! If you're ready,
let's start heading to the field!

235
00:21:21,259 --> 00:21:22,469
What's with him?

236
00:21:24,096 --> 00:21:25,472
Wait for me!

237
00:21:26,014 --> 00:21:27,933
HARVEST BEGINS

238
00:21:28,016 --> 00:21:32,312
<i>It has nothing to do with you</i>

239
00:21:32,396 --> 00:21:37,484
<i>You never existed from the start</i>

240
00:21:40,612 --> 00:21:45,242
Gosh, please do your best to harvest these
for my son-in-law's <i>makgeolli!</i>

241
00:21:45,325 --> 00:21:46,952
-Sure!
-Of course!

242
00:21:47,035 --> 00:21:48,870
Don't worry about it!

243
00:21:48,954 --> 00:21:52,374
My son-in-law's <i>makgeolli</i> business
is going to be a huge success.

244
00:21:52,457 --> 00:21:54,376
The <i>makgeolli </i>will be a big hit!

245
00:21:55,043 --> 00:21:56,086
-A big hit!
-It'll be big!

246
00:21:57,379 --> 00:21:59,589
The <i>makgeolli </i>will be a big hit!

247
00:22:01,758 --> 00:22:02,968
There we go.

248
00:22:06,138 --> 00:22:08,181
This one's huge.

249
00:22:18,108 --> 00:22:19,359
It's so hot.

250
00:22:20,318 --> 00:22:21,236
This is exhausting.

251
00:22:21,319 --> 00:22:22,654
DEOKPUNG CORNFIELD
SUPER SWEET CORN

252
00:22:22,737 --> 00:22:25,782
I feel like I'm going to melt.

253
00:22:27,784 --> 00:22:28,994
I can't do this anymore.

254
00:22:29,536 --> 00:22:31,413
I can't. This is killing me.

255
00:22:31,997 --> 00:22:33,331
I'm so exhausted.

256
00:22:50,348 --> 00:22:51,266
I can do it.

257
00:22:52,225 --> 00:22:53,101
It's doable.

258
00:22:53,935 --> 00:22:54,936
I can do it.

259
00:23:15,040 --> 00:23:16,625
It's time for some snacks.

260
00:23:16,708 --> 00:23:19,377
-Let's go have some snacks.
-Is it time already?

261
00:23:19,461 --> 00:23:21,046
Let's go have snacks.

262
00:23:23,882 --> 00:23:25,258
Eat up, everyone!

263
00:23:25,342 --> 00:23:27,385
Let's eat!

264
00:23:28,887 --> 00:23:30,972
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

265
00:23:36,186 --> 00:23:37,646
They're all carbs.

266
00:23:39,189 --> 00:23:40,106
This is so refreshing.

267
00:23:40,190 --> 00:23:41,942
Sweetie, aren't you eating?

268
00:23:42,025 --> 00:23:44,736
No, ma'am. I have to lose weight.

269
00:23:44,819 --> 00:23:47,614
You eat snacks to keep your energy up.

270
00:23:47,697 --> 00:23:50,200
It's fine.
I usually don't eat much anyway.

271
00:23:50,283 --> 00:23:52,369
Come on. Have a bite.

272
00:23:52,452 --> 00:23:53,912
-It's really fine--
-Just one.

273
00:23:55,705 --> 00:23:57,207
Ma'am!

274
00:23:57,290 --> 00:23:59,584
It's okay.
Delicious food doesn't count. Eat up.

275
00:23:59,668 --> 00:24:00,919
You'll be fine.

276
00:24:05,298 --> 00:24:06,216
Eat up.

277
00:24:18,728 --> 00:24:19,813
It's so good!

278
00:24:19,896 --> 00:24:20,730
DELICIOUS

279
00:24:32,701 --> 00:24:34,202
That was so good!

280
00:24:35,036 --> 00:24:38,915
A refreshing iced Americano
would wash it all down perfectly, right?

281
00:24:38,999 --> 00:24:40,125
Right…

282
00:24:40,208 --> 00:24:42,627
Have some iced coffee, everyone!

283
00:24:43,169 --> 00:24:44,296
Jin-yi!

284
00:24:44,379 --> 00:24:45,714
Hi!

285
00:24:46,298 --> 00:24:47,507
Who is she?

286
00:24:47,590 --> 00:24:49,175
She's the face of Deokpung.

287
00:24:49,259 --> 00:24:51,136
We wouldn't be able to live without her.

288
00:24:51,219 --> 00:24:53,555
This, this, and this.

289
00:24:53,638 --> 00:24:55,223
I bought all these from her shop.

290
00:24:55,307 --> 00:24:56,725
-These too.
-These too.

291
00:25:00,103 --> 00:25:00,937
All right.

292
00:25:03,523 --> 00:25:04,441
Ta-da.

293
00:25:05,692 --> 00:25:07,110
That's refreshing!

294
00:25:07,193 --> 00:25:08,528
Everyone, take one!

295
00:25:09,696 --> 00:25:11,031
It's iced coffee.

296
00:25:11,114 --> 00:25:13,074
She's my sister. Isn't she pretty?

297
00:25:13,158 --> 00:25:15,076
She's got a great personality too.

298
00:25:15,160 --> 00:25:16,828
Som-yi! What are you doing here?

299
00:25:18,038 --> 00:25:19,539
I'll take back that last part.

300
00:25:20,248 --> 00:25:21,541
You little…

301
00:25:21,624 --> 00:25:22,459
Ae-ra.

302
00:25:23,835 --> 00:25:25,337
Would you like to join me?

303
00:25:27,922 --> 00:25:29,007
How cute.

304
00:25:30,300 --> 00:25:31,634
She's always rejecting me.

305
00:25:31,718 --> 00:25:33,011
Are you still trying to woo her?

306
00:25:33,094 --> 00:25:34,846
I wouldn't accept you
if I were her either.

307
00:25:37,223 --> 00:25:39,642
You know we're harvesting
the super sweet corn today.

308
00:25:39,726 --> 00:25:41,644
I told you I wouldn't buy them
for that price.

309
00:25:41,728 --> 00:25:43,521
I can't give them to you
for half the price.

310
00:25:43,605 --> 00:25:44,439
Then…

311
00:25:44,522 --> 00:25:45,815
I have nothing more to say.

312
00:25:45,899 --> 00:25:48,526
I even refused offers
from department stores

313
00:25:48,610 --> 00:25:50,528
to provide them
for your <i>makgeolli</i> factory.

314
00:25:50,612 --> 00:25:52,155
You can't just suddenly do this.

315
00:25:53,239 --> 00:25:54,991
Then, we'll take the penalty fees

316
00:25:55,075 --> 00:25:57,202
and terminate our business
with your factory.

317
00:26:00,205 --> 00:26:01,122
Mechoori.

318
00:26:02,415 --> 00:26:04,042
Sir, please don't…

319
00:26:04,125 --> 00:26:05,585
Can't you let this slide?

320
00:26:06,336 --> 00:26:08,463
My sales are declining,

321
00:26:08,546 --> 00:26:10,465
and my staff are quitting one by one.

322
00:26:12,592 --> 00:26:15,553
I'm even doing deliveries myself now!

323
00:26:16,054 --> 00:26:17,347
To be honest,

324
00:26:17,430 --> 00:26:19,516
I asked for half price
and expected you to refuse.

325
00:26:22,602 --> 00:26:25,814
Does your mother-in-law know
the business isn't doing well?

326
00:26:26,398 --> 00:26:29,150
Please keep this a secret from her.

327
00:26:32,153 --> 00:26:35,573
My son-in-law said he won't buy the corn?

328
00:26:35,657 --> 00:26:39,452
Yes. He's developing a new product,
so we'll have to sell them somewhere else.

329
00:26:39,536 --> 00:26:41,329
Why refuse such good-quality corn?

330
00:26:41,413 --> 00:26:43,081
What about all this corn then?

331
00:26:44,749 --> 00:26:47,502
It'll be fine.
I'll find another way to deal with them.

332
00:26:47,585 --> 00:26:49,379
Let's end work here today.

333
00:26:49,462 --> 00:26:51,089
Thank you, everyone.

334
00:26:51,172 --> 00:26:52,674
They won't taste good at all

335
00:26:52,757 --> 00:26:55,927
if they're not picked
within the next two days.

336
00:26:56,010 --> 00:26:57,137
Right.

337
00:26:57,220 --> 00:26:58,763
Oh, dear.

338
00:26:58,847 --> 00:27:01,099
Ma'am, I'll take you home.

339
00:27:01,182 --> 00:27:03,226
Forget it! I'll pick them all before I go.

340
00:27:04,644 --> 00:27:05,603
Ma'am…

341
00:27:05,687 --> 00:27:07,188
There's nowhere to store them anyway,

342
00:27:07,272 --> 00:27:08,982
and it's better
to keep them on the stalks.

343
00:27:09,065 --> 00:27:11,568
So go and get some rest today.
I'll think about what to do.

344
00:27:36,551 --> 00:27:37,635
So…

345
00:27:37,719 --> 00:27:41,139
all this corn might go to waste.

346
00:27:42,474 --> 00:27:44,309
You should head back too.

347
00:27:45,018 --> 00:27:46,186
Thanks for helping.

348
00:27:46,269 --> 00:27:48,771
I want to help find a solution.

349
00:27:48,855 --> 00:27:51,691
It's fine. I can find another client.

350
00:27:51,774 --> 00:27:53,610
With fresh produce, time is everything.

351
00:27:53,693 --> 00:27:55,612
They're drying out even as we speak.

352
00:27:55,695 --> 00:27:57,489
This has nothing to do with you.

353
00:27:58,990 --> 00:28:01,910
I helped pick these as I suffered
in the scorching sun too.

354
00:28:01,993 --> 00:28:03,828
But they're about to go to waste.

355
00:28:03,912 --> 00:28:05,914
How can I just leave?
Everyone worked so hard.

356
00:28:06,748 --> 00:28:07,999
I can't just go.

357
00:28:14,422 --> 00:28:15,256
Let's sell them.

358
00:28:16,382 --> 00:28:17,217
What?

359
00:28:17,300 --> 00:28:20,136
Let's sell them through a livestream.

360
00:28:21,721 --> 00:28:22,847
Why would you do that?

361
00:28:22,931 --> 00:28:24,974
My nickname is <i>Live Info Show.</i>

362
00:28:25,058 --> 00:28:26,726
I host with life info from the field.

363
00:28:26,809 --> 00:28:27,644
So?

364
00:28:27,727 --> 00:28:28,853
"So?"

365
00:28:29,771 --> 00:28:32,315
You might not realize what this means,

366
00:28:32,398 --> 00:28:34,150
but this is an incredible offer.

367
00:28:38,238 --> 00:28:40,365
Are you not confident about their quality?

368
00:28:43,493 --> 00:28:45,995
The corn here averages 20 Brix.

369
00:28:46,079 --> 00:28:47,205
Do you know what that means?

370
00:28:47,288 --> 00:28:49,207
They're as sweet as top-quality apples,

371
00:28:49,290 --> 00:28:52,293
so they're 100 times more prone
to pests than regular corn,

372
00:28:52,377 --> 00:28:54,212
but we only used natural fertilizer.

373
00:28:55,129 --> 00:28:58,508
Yes. That's why I made such a big decision
as Korea's top home shopping host.

374
00:28:59,259 --> 00:29:01,010
Gather all the elders again.

375
00:29:05,765 --> 00:29:06,724
Hey, Mr. Hwang.

376
00:29:06,808 --> 00:29:09,102
Can you give me the number
of the online department head?

377
00:29:10,186 --> 00:29:12,272
-Where do you want this?
-I'll check for you!

378
00:29:13,064 --> 00:29:14,315
Yes, right there.

379
00:29:14,399 --> 00:29:18,361
FRESH AND STEAMED SUPER SWEET CORN
NATIONWIDE DELIVERY AVAILABLE

380
00:29:19,571 --> 00:29:21,573
DAM YE-JIN'S FIRST
LIVESTREAM SHOPPING BROADCAST

381
00:29:24,909 --> 00:29:26,494
You two stay in the field,

382
00:29:26,578 --> 00:29:30,206
and when the camera comes in,
pick a nice, plump one and bite into it.

383
00:29:32,041 --> 00:29:34,502
Ma'am, you can cook
anything you want with the corn here.

384
00:29:34,586 --> 00:29:35,545
All right.

385
00:29:35,628 --> 00:29:36,963
-Okay!
-Okay!

386
00:29:40,425 --> 00:29:41,885
Our talented director.

387
00:29:41,968 --> 00:29:44,429
Zoom right in on me
when I'm trying the corn later.

388
00:29:44,512 --> 00:29:48,182
I won't lose you even if you
suddenly run off, so do whatever you want!

389
00:29:51,477 --> 00:29:53,730
I found a warehouse
that can handle up to 3,000 boxes.

390
00:29:54,480 --> 00:29:55,440
Three thousand boxes…

391
00:29:55,523 --> 00:29:57,275
Okay! I'll sell them all in ten minutes.

392
00:29:57,358 --> 00:29:58,234
Hang on.

393
00:29:58,318 --> 00:30:01,279
Ms. Dam, are you going to do
the live in that outfit?

394
00:30:01,863 --> 00:30:03,531
This will be aired nationwide.

395
00:30:04,616 --> 00:30:07,243
What other outfit
could be better for selling corn?

396
00:30:07,327 --> 00:30:09,162
Well, it's fine with me.

397
00:30:12,332 --> 00:30:14,375
I'm refreshing the page.

398
00:30:14,459 --> 00:30:15,919
LIMITED OFFER FOR JUST TODAY!

399
00:30:17,086 --> 00:30:18,004
Look at that!

400
00:30:19,172 --> 00:30:20,465
We did it!

401
00:30:20,548 --> 00:30:22,175
We can do the live now!

402
00:30:27,305 --> 00:30:28,973
-There's ten minutes left.
-Right.

403
00:30:29,724 --> 00:30:30,558
Let's go.

404
00:30:34,187 --> 00:30:36,189
DEOKPUNG COMMUNITY CENTER

405
00:30:38,650 --> 00:30:39,943
Come on, hurry.

406
00:30:40,026 --> 00:30:41,402
We don't have time.

407
00:30:48,826 --> 00:30:49,827
What is this?

408
00:30:50,495 --> 00:30:52,121
You didn't know either, did you?

409
00:30:53,915 --> 00:30:56,542
You ran in here to tell me this?
Were you excited to tattle?

410
00:30:56,626 --> 00:30:59,337
Just yesterday, she was desperate
about keeping her time slot.

411
00:30:59,420 --> 00:31:02,048
But now, she's suddenly doing
a livestream shopping broadcast.

412
00:31:02,131 --> 00:31:03,716
She's selling corn.

413
00:31:05,510 --> 00:31:08,721
She caught up with you
even after that incident five years ago.

414
00:31:09,347 --> 00:31:10,264
Ms. Dong.

415
00:31:11,057 --> 00:31:13,393
Dam Ye-jin is the face of HIT.

416
00:31:14,143 --> 00:31:16,145
This affects HIT's image.

417
00:31:17,021 --> 00:31:17,939
Image?

418
00:31:18,940 --> 00:31:21,734
She's selling high-quality products
at a reasonable price.

419
00:31:21,818 --> 00:31:25,029
I think she's maintaining our image
properly as a home shopping host.

420
00:31:25,113 --> 00:31:27,865
You're just going to let her
do whatever she pleases?

421
00:31:27,949 --> 00:31:28,908
All I'm looking for

422
00:31:29,867 --> 00:31:30,785
is survival.

423
00:31:32,245 --> 00:31:33,162
Yun-ji.

424
00:31:33,246 --> 00:31:35,456
Stop acting all high and mighty

425
00:31:36,374 --> 00:31:38,292
and think about how to survive.

426
00:31:39,043 --> 00:31:41,963
Hello, everyone.
I'm home shopping host Dam Ye-jin.

427
00:31:42,046 --> 00:31:44,549
You must be wondering what I'm doing here.

428
00:31:44,632 --> 00:31:46,634
Starting now, for 30 minutes…

429
00:31:47,427 --> 00:31:52,015
For just 30 minutes, I'm going to offer
super sweet corn from Deokpung Village.

430
00:31:52,098 --> 00:31:55,852
With ten ears of corn per box,
there's a total of 3,000 boxes.

431
00:31:55,935 --> 00:31:58,604
This is a limited-time offer sale
for these 3,000 boxes!

432
00:31:59,439 --> 00:32:00,273
DEOKPUNG CORNFIELD

433
00:32:00,356 --> 00:32:03,234
We'll be delivering fresh corn
straight from Deokpung Village,

434
00:32:03,317 --> 00:32:05,111
the place where they were grown.

435
00:32:05,194 --> 00:32:06,279
SUPER SWEET CORN

436
00:32:06,362 --> 00:32:08,239
So make your orders now.

437
00:32:08,823 --> 00:32:11,826
I see the farmers working hard
to harvest the corn right now.

438
00:32:11,909 --> 00:32:13,327
How about a brief interview?

439
00:32:13,411 --> 00:32:14,912
Hello, sirs.

440
00:32:14,996 --> 00:32:16,581
-Hello.
-Hello.

441
00:32:16,664 --> 00:32:18,541
Can you show us the corn?

442
00:32:18,624 --> 00:32:20,043
The corn?

443
00:32:20,126 --> 00:32:21,252
All right.

444
00:32:21,919 --> 00:32:23,171
There we go!

445
00:32:23,254 --> 00:32:27,091
We didn't use any pesticides,
so you can eat it raw.

446
00:32:27,175 --> 00:32:29,886
I'll try to make
an acrostic poem with corn.

447
00:32:29,969 --> 00:32:31,637
-C!
-Completely tasty.

448
00:32:31,721 --> 00:32:33,139
-OR!
-Oh, right. It goes right down.

449
00:32:33,222 --> 00:32:35,892
-N!
-Nice… and refreshing alcohol!

450
00:32:35,975 --> 00:32:37,060
-Super sweet--
-You idiot.

451
00:32:37,143 --> 00:32:40,772
Everyone, look at how plump
these kernels are.

452
00:32:40,855 --> 00:32:43,691
This ear of corn is
as big as my arm, isn't it?

453
00:32:44,192 --> 00:32:46,402
They're delicious
even if you eat them raw,

454
00:32:46,486 --> 00:32:49,030
but there are a variety
of ways to enjoy them.

455
00:32:49,113 --> 00:32:50,448
Shall we take a look?

456
00:32:50,531 --> 00:32:51,532
Hello!

457
00:32:51,616 --> 00:32:53,242
What is this?

458
00:32:53,326 --> 00:32:55,870
This is a tasty corn pancake!

459
00:32:55,953 --> 00:32:57,789
Corn pancakes?

460
00:32:57,872 --> 00:32:59,874
And this is corn salad.

461
00:33:01,292 --> 00:33:04,754
Even if you're not a good cook,
there's no need to worry.

462
00:33:04,837 --> 00:33:07,298
It still tastes incredible
if you eat them raw.

463
00:33:09,050 --> 00:33:12,303
They're as sweet as fruit.
Let me offer our cameraman a bite too.

464
00:33:12,386 --> 00:33:13,304
3,000 BOXES SOLD OUT

465
00:33:15,223 --> 00:33:16,265
Sold out.

466
00:33:17,141 --> 00:33:18,101
Sold out!

467
00:33:18,184 --> 00:33:20,394
We sold out!

468
00:33:22,188 --> 00:33:26,984
Thank you for showing us so much support
despite this being an unexpected live.

469
00:33:27,068 --> 00:33:30,655
All right, I'll see you again
tomorrow evening on <i>It's a HIT!</i>

470
00:33:30,738 --> 00:33:32,824
Thank you for all your love today.

471
00:33:32,907 --> 00:33:35,493
This has been Dam Ye-jin. Thank you!

472
00:33:35,576 --> 00:33:36,702
Cut!

473
00:33:39,997 --> 00:33:41,624
We sold out!

474
00:33:41,707 --> 00:33:43,876
Sold out! We sold out!

475
00:33:44,836 --> 00:33:46,170
Ms. Yang!

476
00:33:46,254 --> 00:33:50,424
Thank heavens!
Thank you, God! Thank you, Buddha!

477
00:33:51,008 --> 00:33:54,095
You're my granddaughter now, sweetie.

478
00:33:54,178 --> 00:33:56,681
It's only because
the corn was such high-quality.

479
00:33:56,764 --> 00:33:58,808
Not because you're pretty?

480
00:33:59,600 --> 00:34:01,853
Come here, everyone!
Let's take a selfie together!

481
00:34:01,936 --> 00:34:03,062
Look here!

482
00:34:05,982 --> 00:34:07,275
Mechoori!

483
00:34:07,358 --> 00:34:10,361
We have no time.
We have to harvest 3,000 boxes of corn!

484
00:34:11,028 --> 00:34:12,530
-Let's get to work.
-All right.

485
00:34:12,613 --> 00:34:15,199
-I'll call everyone who's free.
-Me too.

486
00:34:15,283 --> 00:34:18,411
You don't have any friends.
Just go and start picking.

487
00:34:21,747 --> 00:34:22,832
Sweetie!

488
00:34:25,751 --> 00:34:26,669
Ms. Dam.

489
00:34:30,423 --> 00:34:31,507
Ms. Dam?

490
00:34:33,009 --> 00:34:33,926
Are you awake?

491
00:34:41,267 --> 00:34:42,602
Mr. Mechoori?

492
00:34:44,770 --> 00:34:45,938
Ms. Dam.

493
00:34:46,522 --> 00:34:48,608
Can you recognize me?

494
00:34:48,691 --> 00:34:50,860
Can you recognize me or not?

495
00:34:51,777 --> 00:34:53,779
Gosh, this is terrible!

496
00:34:53,863 --> 00:34:54,739
Ms. Dam.

497
00:34:55,990 --> 00:34:57,366
Ms. Dam!

498
00:34:57,450 --> 00:34:59,452
Are you all right?

499
00:34:59,535 --> 00:35:00,620
Ms. Dam!

500
00:35:00,703 --> 00:35:01,704
Ms. Dam…

501
00:35:03,372 --> 00:35:04,457
What was that?

502
00:35:07,752 --> 00:35:09,378
Ms. Dam. Are you all right?

503
00:35:12,173 --> 00:35:13,466
This is the hospital, right?

504
00:35:14,258 --> 00:35:17,011
Unbelievable.
This is the first time I've ever fainted.

505
00:35:17,094 --> 00:35:17,970
Right…

506
00:35:19,305 --> 00:35:23,184
Did I get carried here
like in a romance movie?

507
00:35:24,685 --> 00:35:25,728
Well…

508
00:35:28,147 --> 00:35:32,401
I thought that was all made up,
but I guess it's real.

509
00:35:32,485 --> 00:35:36,447
When I saw scenes like that
in romance movies,

510
00:35:37,490 --> 00:35:40,284
I thought they were exaggerating.

511
00:35:42,286 --> 00:35:43,913
But it was real.

512
00:35:46,207 --> 00:35:47,291
Jung-muk.

513
00:35:47,375 --> 00:35:49,502
I don't think
Ms. Dam is in her right mind.

514
00:35:49,585 --> 00:35:51,921
-This feels so familiar.
-She seems possessed.

515
00:35:52,421 --> 00:35:54,924
What if she's about to die?

516
00:35:55,007 --> 00:35:56,884
Jung-muk! Come and check!

517
00:35:56,968 --> 00:35:58,511
It's just heatstroke.

518
00:35:58,594 --> 00:36:00,221
People don't die that easily.

519
00:36:04,267 --> 00:36:06,143
So this is what it's like.

520
00:36:07,270 --> 00:36:08,771
WOORI DEOKPUNG MEDICAL CLINIC

521
00:36:08,854 --> 00:36:10,231
It's heatstroke.

522
00:36:10,314 --> 00:36:12,400
No, it was from being out in the sun.

523
00:36:13,484 --> 00:36:15,569
Yeah. She'll get better after some rest.

524
00:36:17,321 --> 00:36:20,283
But who is she? You seem so worried.

525
00:36:20,992 --> 00:36:22,243
It's nothing.

526
00:36:22,326 --> 00:36:24,203
All right. Bye.

527
00:36:33,087 --> 00:36:34,255
Hey, Mechoori.

528
00:36:39,760 --> 00:36:40,720
What is this?

529
00:36:45,891 --> 00:36:47,393
Why are you giving me so much?

530
00:36:47,476 --> 00:36:49,729
I said it was only half price
to use the warehouse.

531
00:36:49,812 --> 00:36:52,106
I can't accept this much.

532
00:36:52,189 --> 00:36:54,817
I'm giving Ms. Yang
one less thing to worry about.

533
00:36:55,484 --> 00:36:58,821
And your <i>makgeolli</i>
is like medicine for the elders here.

534
00:36:58,904 --> 00:37:00,323
It'd be a disaster if it was gone.

535
00:37:00,990 --> 00:37:02,533
And remember not to skip your meals.

536
00:37:05,536 --> 00:37:06,454
Mechoori.

537
00:37:06,537 --> 00:37:08,622
DEOKPUNG SUPER SWEET CORN
MAKGEOLLI BREWERY

538
00:37:08,706 --> 00:37:12,251
Gosh, our little quail is so kind.

539
00:37:12,335 --> 00:37:14,670
Let's go inside and sleep now. Okay.

540
00:37:15,504 --> 00:37:17,298
There you go. It's okay. Get some sleep.

541
00:37:19,008 --> 00:37:19,925
Hey, Dad.

542
00:37:20,509 --> 00:37:22,887
Hey. What happened?

543
00:37:22,970 --> 00:37:25,222
Is she okay? Is she awake? How is she?

544
00:37:25,306 --> 00:37:26,390
She had heatstroke.

545
00:37:26,474 --> 00:37:28,392
She's Mechoori's girlfriend, right?

546
00:37:28,476 --> 00:37:29,310
Girlfriend?

547
00:37:30,269 --> 00:37:31,354
What?

548
00:37:31,437 --> 00:37:33,522
It seems like
you're the one who got heatstroke.

549
00:37:34,023 --> 00:37:35,441
SALES COMMISSION AGREEMENT

550
00:37:36,192 --> 00:37:37,318
My goodness.

551
00:37:38,319 --> 00:37:40,279
I told you I don't need
any of the profits.

552
00:37:42,740 --> 00:37:45,493
You're receiving it fair and square,
so don't feel bad about it.

553
00:37:46,744 --> 00:37:47,953
You know,

554
00:37:48,037 --> 00:37:50,289
this is a complicated way
of saying thank you.

555
00:37:58,964 --> 00:38:00,299
-What?
-Aren't you leaving?

556
00:38:00,883 --> 00:38:02,218
I was just about to.

557
00:38:11,435 --> 00:38:12,645
Hang on.

558
00:38:12,728 --> 00:38:15,272
What's going on?
Why am I suddenly so dizzy?

559
00:38:15,356 --> 00:38:16,357
Just a moment.

560
00:38:19,777 --> 00:38:22,488
Hold on, I'm seriously not faking this.

561
00:38:23,280 --> 00:38:24,198
What's wrong with me?

562
00:38:25,991 --> 00:38:27,410
I need to lie down. Hang on.

563
00:38:29,203 --> 00:38:30,037
Just a moment.

564
00:38:34,375 --> 00:38:35,376
Are you serious?

565
00:38:35,459 --> 00:38:38,212
I can't even hold my head up.

566
00:38:39,672 --> 00:38:42,925
I have some salt and glucose tablets
in my bag over there.

567
00:38:43,008 --> 00:38:44,343
Could you get them for me?

568
00:38:47,263 --> 00:38:49,890
You can just empty out my bag.

569
00:38:49,974 --> 00:38:51,976
It's an emergency. I'm sorry.

570
00:38:52,059 --> 00:38:53,394
Why is my head spinning?

571
00:38:57,690 --> 00:38:58,774
Yes, I think that's it.

572
00:38:58,858 --> 00:38:59,942
It's that one.

573
00:39:01,444 --> 00:39:02,820
This is killing me.

574
00:39:06,907 --> 00:39:07,908
This is so strange.

575
00:39:11,579 --> 00:39:12,538
Gosh, my head.

576
00:39:15,291 --> 00:39:16,125
Get up.

577
00:39:16,792 --> 00:39:18,002
Gosh.

578
00:39:19,587 --> 00:39:20,629
Thank you.

579
00:39:27,303 --> 00:39:28,220
Gosh.

580
00:39:28,804 --> 00:39:29,680
Hang on.

581
00:39:32,933 --> 00:39:34,852
Why are you so set
on overworking yourself?

582
00:39:36,604 --> 00:39:37,730
Me?

583
00:39:37,813 --> 00:39:41,400
You don't treat your injuries properly
and get heatstroke after working too hard.

584
00:39:43,194 --> 00:39:44,111
I know, right?

585
00:39:44,987 --> 00:39:48,365
Who do you think is the cause of all that?

586
00:39:51,160 --> 00:39:54,413
Whatever you do,
nothing's going to change.

587
00:39:55,414 --> 00:39:56,499
So stop wasting your time.

588
00:40:00,252 --> 00:40:01,712
Hey, I'm sick.

589
00:40:02,838 --> 00:40:04,840
You're hurting me more with these truths.

590
00:40:08,552 --> 00:40:09,386
Hey.

591
00:40:10,221 --> 00:40:13,015
Let me rest a bit on your sofa.

592
00:40:13,098 --> 00:40:14,725
I really can't move right now.

593
00:40:15,601 --> 00:40:16,810
Just a second.

594
00:40:17,603 --> 00:40:18,896
Wait.

595
00:40:22,525 --> 00:40:23,609
Stay still.

596
00:40:34,036 --> 00:40:34,954
Why?

597
00:40:41,043 --> 00:40:42,127
You're crumpling up my rug.

598
00:40:54,390 --> 00:40:55,349
Gosh.

599
00:40:56,225 --> 00:40:58,310
Why is it so far away? It's killing me.

600
00:41:04,358 --> 00:41:05,693
I'll just rest here.

601
00:41:44,857 --> 00:41:46,233
Gosh, my head.

602
00:41:46,942 --> 00:41:49,862
I told you I have a headache.

603
00:41:51,655 --> 00:41:52,823
My head…

604
00:41:54,199 --> 00:41:55,159
Geez.

605
00:41:56,410 --> 00:41:58,078
He's such a weirdo.

606
00:42:39,286 --> 00:42:41,622
What? Hey, where's my shirt?

607
00:42:44,416 --> 00:42:50,214
<i>Now, I'll just let myself</i>

608
00:42:50,297 --> 00:42:53,384
<i>Go with the flow</i>

609
00:42:53,467 --> 00:42:55,719
<i>It has nothing to do…</i>

610
00:42:55,803 --> 00:42:57,554
What?

611
00:42:57,638 --> 00:42:58,472
What is that?

612
00:43:02,935 --> 00:43:04,186
No. Please.

613
00:43:07,398 --> 00:43:09,274
Please back up.

614
00:43:15,280 --> 00:43:16,365
Damn it!

615
00:43:22,121 --> 00:43:23,872
I'm busy.

616
00:43:25,999 --> 00:43:27,376
What? What is this?

617
00:43:39,096 --> 00:43:41,682
Sir, let me pass.

618
00:43:41,765 --> 00:43:43,350
Can you move your vehicle?

619
00:43:57,656 --> 00:43:59,408
What are you doing?

620
00:43:59,491 --> 00:44:00,784
I said move your car!

621
00:44:01,952 --> 00:44:04,329
It seems like
this is your first time here.

622
00:44:04,413 --> 00:44:06,790
But this is a one-way street.

623
00:44:08,584 --> 00:44:10,502
There's no such thing on a farm road!

624
00:44:10,586 --> 00:44:12,629
I've come all the way in.
I have the right of way!

625
00:44:12,713 --> 00:44:14,339
You know what? Forget it.

626
00:44:16,175 --> 00:44:19,011
This is the way out!

627
00:44:25,851 --> 00:44:27,478
He has a weird look.

628
00:44:27,561 --> 00:44:29,396
I have to back up. I should go.

629
00:44:34,318 --> 00:44:35,194
What was that?

630
00:44:36,653 --> 00:44:39,323
Damn it, it's stuck!

631
00:44:39,406 --> 00:44:40,866
Wait. Hold on.

632
00:44:50,083 --> 00:44:51,043
Come on…

633
00:44:52,169 --> 00:44:53,003
No.

634
00:44:53,086 --> 00:44:54,296
Hey, that lunatic is coming.

635
00:44:54,379 --> 00:44:56,507
Please, come on…

636
00:44:57,674 --> 00:44:59,551
Listen, I was just about to back up…

637
00:45:05,974 --> 00:45:07,142
Where is he going?

638
00:45:07,768 --> 00:45:10,771
Wait. What is he doing?

639
00:45:46,056 --> 00:45:47,558
I'll back up for you this time.

640
00:45:48,892 --> 00:45:49,977
Go on.

641
00:46:04,408 --> 00:46:06,743
Who the hell is this potato-looking guy?

642
00:46:06,827 --> 00:46:10,289
Get it together, you lunatic!
Are you crazy?

643
00:46:38,150 --> 00:46:39,359
What are you taking home?

644
00:46:40,485 --> 00:46:41,903
A car, of course.

645
00:46:41,987 --> 00:46:43,530
You're driving in that condition?

646
00:46:44,531 --> 00:46:45,699
Gosh, I'm so touched.

647
00:46:45,782 --> 00:46:47,409
Are you worried about me?

648
00:46:48,118 --> 00:46:49,578
If you feel bad,

649
00:46:49,661 --> 00:46:52,289
then take a look at the documents
I left on your table.

650
00:46:53,123 --> 00:46:53,999
Goodbye, then.

651
00:47:01,131 --> 00:47:03,800
What's going on? Who is that?

652
00:47:05,552 --> 00:47:06,928
Who is it? Who?

653
00:47:10,849 --> 00:47:12,768
-Let's go now.
-I won't let this slide.

654
00:47:32,329 --> 00:47:34,998
<i>I can sell the essence</i>
<i>even better than the corn.</i>

655
00:47:43,298 --> 00:47:45,175
That guy back there was him, wasn't it?

656
00:47:45,967 --> 00:47:47,177
From Gojeuneok whatever?

657
00:47:49,596 --> 00:47:51,264
I should've given him a piece of my mind.

658
00:47:51,890 --> 00:47:52,724
Why?

659
00:47:54,893 --> 00:47:57,396
He made you work until you got heatstroke.

660
00:47:57,479 --> 00:47:59,606
Not even dogs are trained that harshly!

661
00:47:59,690 --> 00:48:01,274
So he thinks he can boss you around?

662
00:48:01,358 --> 00:48:02,567
He's not like that.

663
00:48:07,114 --> 00:48:08,198
What's with you?

664
00:48:10,075 --> 00:48:10,951
What?

665
00:48:16,456 --> 00:48:18,500
Dam Ye-jin. Go in and get some rest.

666
00:48:18,583 --> 00:48:19,418
Okay.

667
00:48:19,501 --> 00:48:20,836
Don't do anything and just sleep.

668
00:48:20,919 --> 00:48:22,671
Okay, already. Go on.

669
00:48:22,754 --> 00:48:23,588
Bye.

670
00:48:23,672 --> 00:48:25,549
-Bye.
-Drive safe.

671
00:48:31,596 --> 00:48:32,472
I'm so tired.

672
00:48:37,018 --> 00:48:38,353
Goodness.

673
00:48:38,437 --> 00:48:41,898
Ye-jin, get a grip. This isn't the time.

674
00:48:44,192 --> 00:48:45,902
I need some caffeine in my blood.

675
00:48:50,991 --> 00:48:52,534
I made an order by phone.

676
00:48:52,617 --> 00:48:53,618
Just a moment, please.

677
00:48:53,702 --> 00:48:54,619
All right.

678
00:49:00,167 --> 00:49:01,835
-Here you go.
-Right.

679
00:49:03,754 --> 00:49:06,298
-Thank you.
-Thank you. Have a nice night.

680
00:49:09,342 --> 00:49:10,594
Thank you.

681
00:49:12,304 --> 00:49:13,597
Can I trust you on the taste?

682
00:49:13,680 --> 00:49:16,099
It's from a coffee shop
that Dam Ye-jin frequents,

683
00:49:16,183 --> 00:49:17,434
so it'll be good.

684
00:49:17,517 --> 00:49:19,478
-Dam Ye-jin?
-Yes.

685
00:49:19,561 --> 00:49:21,271
She was just at the coffee shop.

686
00:49:22,606 --> 00:49:24,524
Really? The coffee shop?

687
00:49:24,608 --> 00:49:27,277
Mr. Cha, you can head home now.

688
00:49:27,360 --> 00:49:30,113
The coffee smells so good
that I don't want to work late.

689
00:49:31,615 --> 00:49:34,075
You've been working so hard
without getting any rest.

690
00:49:34,159 --> 00:49:36,119
-Right.
-Get a lot of rest tonight.

691
00:49:36,203 --> 00:49:37,913
-I should get some sleep.
-And tomorrow…

692
00:49:37,996 --> 00:49:40,165
-Okay, all right. Go home now.
-With a relaxed mind…

693
00:49:40,248 --> 00:49:41,124
Go on. Good night!

694
00:49:41,208 --> 00:49:42,793
-Before bed…
-No, it's okay.

695
00:49:42,876 --> 00:49:44,795
-Good night!
-…massage your feet…

696
00:50:08,276 --> 00:50:09,611
What a coincidence.

697
00:50:11,238 --> 00:50:12,280
Mr. Seo.

698
00:50:12,781 --> 00:50:14,241
Did you come here for coffee?

699
00:50:14,324 --> 00:50:16,535
I came here to work.

700
00:50:17,577 --> 00:50:19,913
The espresso here is really good.

701
00:50:19,996 --> 00:50:20,997
I highly recommend it.

702
00:50:21,957 --> 00:50:23,166
I'll give it a try.

703
00:51:29,566 --> 00:51:31,985
Great. It's even raining.

704
00:51:59,054 --> 00:52:00,472
You don't have an umbrella?

705
00:52:01,181 --> 00:52:03,183
Then, should I save you this time?

706
00:52:14,986 --> 00:52:17,113
This is that umbrella, isn't it?

707
00:52:17,739 --> 00:52:18,782
Yes.

708
00:52:18,865 --> 00:52:21,660
It was the item that helped me
get my first-ever sellout.

709
00:52:22,911 --> 00:52:25,205
Try looking around when it rains.

710
00:52:25,288 --> 00:52:27,457
I bet at least one out of ten people
use this umbrella.

711
00:52:27,540 --> 00:52:28,833
Gosh, did you see that?

712
00:52:28,917 --> 00:52:30,335
At this point,

713
00:52:30,418 --> 00:52:32,879
I feel like I should ask you
for a nice meal sometime.

714
00:52:32,963 --> 00:52:34,464
Sure, when you're free--

715
00:52:34,547 --> 00:52:35,382
Tonight.

716
00:52:37,717 --> 00:52:39,386
Treat me to a meal tonight.

717
00:52:41,596 --> 00:52:42,764
What would you like?

718
00:52:45,225 --> 00:52:46,893
How about croissants?

719
00:52:50,730 --> 00:52:52,148
Mr. Seo…

720
00:52:54,484 --> 00:52:57,487
I don't date people I do business with.

721
00:52:58,530 --> 00:53:00,615
When my feelings got involved,

722
00:53:00,699 --> 00:53:03,493
I ended up losing
both my work and my relationship.

723
00:53:07,330 --> 00:53:08,164
All right.

724
00:53:09,332 --> 00:53:10,166
Let's work then.

725
00:53:11,459 --> 00:53:12,877
But once everything is resolved,

726
00:53:13,920 --> 00:53:16,965
let's have a nice meal together.

727
00:53:39,237 --> 00:53:41,448
I can't even hold my head up.

728
00:53:41,531 --> 00:53:43,950
<i>You can just empty out my bag.</i>

729
00:53:46,703 --> 00:53:48,121
OVERUSE IS STRICTLY PROHIBITED

730
00:54:06,264 --> 00:54:07,140
Thank you.

731
00:54:11,978 --> 00:54:14,105
Finally!

732
00:54:14,189 --> 00:54:15,899
You've been through so much, Rose.

733
00:54:15,982 --> 00:54:17,734
I'll treat you better from now on.

734
00:54:23,239 --> 00:54:24,157
Hello, Ms. Yang.

735
00:54:26,284 --> 00:54:27,202
Mr. Mechoori?

736
00:54:30,997 --> 00:54:32,123
What is it?

737
00:54:33,124 --> 00:54:34,292
My meds?

738
00:54:36,002 --> 00:54:38,338
You're right! I'll head over right now.

739
00:54:38,421 --> 00:54:40,590
It's late. Come tomorrow--

740
00:54:40,673 --> 00:54:42,217
No, I'll head over now.

741
00:54:42,300 --> 00:54:44,219
<i>Do you know what time it is right now?</i>

742
00:54:44,302 --> 00:54:46,096
It doesn't matter. Without my meds, I…

743
00:54:49,140 --> 00:54:50,350
<i>All right.</i>

744
00:54:50,433 --> 00:54:51,643
Then, let's meet halfway.

745
00:55:00,318 --> 00:55:02,904
Thank you. Have a good night.

746
00:55:04,364 --> 00:55:05,281
What's going on?

747
00:55:10,078 --> 00:55:12,288
Do you think

748
00:55:12,372 --> 00:55:15,708
I wouldn't notice those rocks
rattling around in your heart?

749
00:55:17,168 --> 00:55:18,086
Mechoori.

750
00:55:19,087 --> 00:55:22,924
Not even the harshest winter winds
can stop the spring breeze.

751
00:55:23,716 --> 00:55:26,219
You can't stop things
that force their way in

752
00:55:26,302 --> 00:55:27,679
no matter how hard you try.

753
00:55:27,762 --> 00:55:29,806
I'm sure you know that.

754
00:55:41,776 --> 00:55:43,611
HIT HOMESHOPPING

755
00:55:43,695 --> 00:55:46,072
SLEEP MEDICATION, SLEEP AID,
ANTI-ANXIETY MEDICATION

756
00:56:00,879 --> 00:56:01,754
Hello?

757
00:56:01,838 --> 00:56:03,173
<i>Hey, Mechoori.</i>

758
00:56:03,256 --> 00:56:05,508
<i>There's an emergency.</i>
<i>Come to the farm right now!</i>

759
00:56:09,971 --> 00:56:12,473
Mechoori, this is a disaster!

760
00:56:14,767 --> 00:56:15,768
What happened?

761
00:56:15,852 --> 00:56:17,812
I heard something, so I came to check,

762
00:56:17,896 --> 00:56:19,564
and this whole place was getting watered.

763
00:56:19,647 --> 00:56:21,983
There must've been an error
with the humidity controls.

764
00:56:22,066 --> 00:56:23,109
What do we do?

765
00:56:25,320 --> 00:56:27,071
We have to wash these quickly.

766
00:56:27,155 --> 00:56:28,907
It's only a matter of time
before they die.

767
00:56:29,407 --> 00:56:31,701
Let's fill
the high-pressure sprayer first.

768
00:56:33,620 --> 00:56:35,997
DEOKCHEON REST AREA

769
00:56:47,467 --> 00:56:49,093
I guess I got here first.

770
00:56:57,352 --> 00:56:58,228
TRASH

771
00:56:58,311 --> 00:56:59,604
I'm sorry.

772
00:57:30,176 --> 00:57:31,135
Where did it…

773
00:57:32,637 --> 00:57:33,721
Where is it?

774
00:57:36,808 --> 00:57:37,767
We have to save them.

775
00:57:45,525 --> 00:57:46,609
What do I do?

776
00:57:50,905 --> 00:57:52,824
Geez, I feel so stupid.

777
00:57:52,907 --> 00:57:53,992
I'm an idiot.

778
00:58:24,689 --> 00:58:25,523
Sung-mi.

779
00:58:27,483 --> 00:58:29,235
I can't pick up right now.

780
00:58:29,319 --> 00:58:31,446
MS. ANGRY EOM

781
00:58:34,907 --> 00:58:35,742
Geez.

782
00:58:52,592 --> 00:58:53,926
What's taking him so long?

783
00:59:32,882 --> 00:59:34,884
Mom said she'd come.

784
00:59:34,967 --> 00:59:36,761
She'll come soon.

785
00:59:43,059 --> 00:59:44,310
It's okay.

786
00:59:46,813 --> 00:59:47,647
It's okay.

787
00:59:52,402 --> 00:59:55,071
Mom said she'd come.

788
00:59:56,489 --> 00:59:58,241
She'll come soon.

789
00:59:58,324 --> 01:00:00,618
-It's okay.
<i>-She'll come soon.</i>

790
01:00:02,495 --> 01:00:03,996
She'll come soon.

791
01:00:10,545 --> 01:00:11,754
It's okay.

792
01:00:14,090 --> 01:00:15,091
It's okay.

793
01:00:16,884 --> 01:00:18,928
It's okay, Ye-jin.

794
01:00:20,096 --> 01:00:21,264
It's okay.

795
01:00:31,691 --> 01:00:32,775
Ms. Dam!

796
01:00:48,666 --> 01:00:49,584
I'm sorry.

797
01:02:20,925 --> 01:02:22,385
Earlier,

798
01:02:23,511 --> 01:02:24,846
well…

799
01:02:26,264 --> 01:02:27,682
it just ended up that way.

800
01:02:32,603 --> 01:02:33,521
I'm sorry I was late.

801
01:02:33,604 --> 01:02:34,438
Exactly.

802
01:02:35,147 --> 01:02:36,858
Do you have any idea what time it is?

803
01:02:36,941 --> 01:02:39,026
I was going to come right away, but--

804
01:02:39,110 --> 01:02:41,487
Forget it. Just give me my meds.

805
01:02:56,294 --> 01:02:57,461
Are you kidding me?

806
01:02:58,838 --> 01:02:59,964
I'll give you one each day.

807
01:03:03,009 --> 01:03:04,760
-What do you think you're doing?
-Ms. Dam.

808
01:03:08,139 --> 01:03:09,599
Let's meet every day.

809
01:03:15,855 --> 01:03:17,023
<i>Mom.</i>

810
01:03:18,107 --> 01:03:20,568
<i>I went to a place called Deokpung Village.</i>

811
01:03:21,861 --> 01:03:25,114
And I met someone really strange.

812
01:03:26,782 --> 01:03:28,784
He's so stubborn,

813
01:03:30,661 --> 01:03:35,291
and he keeps interrupting me when I talk.

814
01:03:38,252 --> 01:03:39,754
But the thing is…

815
01:03:42,048 --> 01:03:43,883
when I'm with him,

816
01:03:45,551 --> 01:03:47,303
I feel like

817
01:03:49,138 --> 01:03:51,140
everything's going to be okay.

818
01:03:54,560 --> 01:03:56,562
So…

819
01:03:58,230 --> 01:03:59,732
would it be okay

820
01:04:00,983 --> 01:04:02,902
to trust him instead of me…

821
01:04:05,196 --> 01:04:07,698
and try this again?

822
01:04:33,307 --> 01:04:37,436
<i>Not even the harshest winter winds</i>
<i>can stop the spring breeze.</i>

823
01:04:40,231 --> 01:04:42,984
<i>You can't stop things</i>
<i>that force their way in</i>

824
01:04:43,985 --> 01:04:45,486
<i>no matter how hard you try.</i>

825
01:04:54,912 --> 01:04:58,624
SOLD OUT ON YOU

826
01:05:28,988 --> 01:05:30,823
<i>Were you with sweetie last night?</i>

827
01:05:30,906 --> 01:05:33,784
<i>I must be out of my mind. I must be crazy.</i>

828
01:05:33,868 --> 01:05:35,244
<i>Ms. Dam will contact you as well.</i>

829
01:05:35,327 --> 01:05:37,455
<i>Please tell me when she contacts you.</i>

830
01:05:37,538 --> 01:05:39,457
Renewal? You're renewing the contract?

831
01:05:40,416 --> 01:05:41,375
<i>Quit this right now.</i>

832
01:05:41,459 --> 01:05:44,128
<i>Ruining my life was enough,</i>
<i>don't you think?</i>

833
01:05:45,296 --> 01:05:47,465
<i>Would you ever consider</i>
<i>working for L'Étoile?</i>

834
01:05:47,548 --> 01:05:51,761
<i>Just think of this as giving Ms. Dam</i>
<i>a tour of this raw material farm.</i>

835
01:05:51,844 --> 01:05:53,929
<i>Today will be</i>
<i>the first and last shoot here.</i>

836
01:05:54,013 --> 01:05:56,265
<i>Then, why did you say yes</i>
<i>instead of refusing?</i>

837
01:05:56,348 --> 01:05:57,933
<i>It was because of you, Ms. Dam.</i>

838
01:06:04,982 --> 01:06:06,984
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park

